m1	146,408,1797,886		Chinese melody after John Barrow, in the treble clef, on three staves of twelve bars with a repeat after the second bar, written in the first scale of five tones, without Third or Seventh.
m2	148,1180,1803,1888		An older form of the Scotch air Cockle Shells, in the treble clef with one flat and common time, on four staves of about sixteen bars; an air of minor character in the second scale, without Second or Sixth.
